- Pseudonymisation at collection: each participant is given a participant number, which labels all research data. Names, email addresses and consent forms are stored separately; a single linking key is held securely by the PI.
{% if d.has_audio %}
- Recordings are transcribed by the research team with names and identifying details (e.g. employers, places) removed, then deleted once the transcript is checked.
{% endif %}
- Anonymisation: {{ p.withdrawal }} after each person's participation the linking key entry is deleted, and the data are fully anonymised.
- Research outputs report group-level results only; quotes are anonymised and used only with consent.
